  strong enough to reach the ether means  he and iris will have to make the  arduous trek to the lake hazen weather  station  which has a stronger antenna and should  be clear of radiation the crew of the  ether also have to make a difficult  decision they've deviated off course and  because their communications aren't  working they'll need to veer off course  in order to pick up signals from the  beacon they placed on k23  this will allow them to recalibrate  their position and get back on course  but it also puts them into unmapped  territory  augustine and iris's journey to lake  hazen is filled with moments that hint  at iris being his daughter like when he  tells her we need  sleep but switches his line to i need  sleep or when he sees her drawing a  picture of what he thinks is her mom  is that your mom i knew her face like  that once  she was as loud as you are quiet iris  silence gets at augustine  oh you should tell me something about  your life but she can't say anything  because he doesn't know anything about  her life he's never made an  effort to be there for her if you wanted  to know about you  you can introduce yourself it's only now  that he's dying and could lose her  forever that this regret  washes over him iris in this sense is a  haunting ghost reminding him  of his failures as a father a few scenes  later augustine loses iris in a blizzard  yelling out that he's here  but he's never been there for her he's  saved by a vision of gene  iris's mother which quickly turns into  that of iris as if the mother-daughter  connection wasn't evident enough  back on the ether the crew must repair  the satellite and communication  equipment  after it was wrecked by flying debris of  ice and rock while navigating the  unmapped territory  this ends in tragedy when another wave  of debris hits the ship and wounds maya  who later succumbs to her injury  and if things couldn't get any worse the  crew get their first image of earth with  swirling bands of radioac